<span id="A7.T12.3.14.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:17.3pt;">
<span id="A7.T12.3.14.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T12.3.14.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#FFECD9;">5</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T12.3.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T12.3.14.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T12.3.14.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T12.3.14.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"># Add a Node Using Search 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## GOAL 
<br class="ltx_break">Use the node search to find and add a Send Email node, configure its subject, and connect it to the end of a pipeline. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## STEPS 
<br class="ltx_break">1. Open the "API Data Pipeline" workflow. 
<br class="ltx_break">2. Use the node search box to find "Send Email". 
<br class="ltx_break">3. Add the "Send Email" node to the canvas after the "Sort" node. 
<br class="ltx_break">4. Set "Send Email" subject to "Users list". 
<br class="ltx_break">5. Connect the "Sort" node output to the "Send Email" node input. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"># RESULT FORMAT 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘json 
<br class="ltx_break">{"answer": "done"} 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T12.3.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T12.3.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFECD9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"></td>
<td id="A7.T12.3.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
