<span id="A7.T13.3.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:17.3pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#D9FFD9;">2</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"># Position Elements Relative to Reference 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## GOAL 
<br class="ltx_break">Open a scene and reposition two elements at a fixed distance from a reference object along the X-axis, preserving their orientations. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## STEPS 
<br class="ltx_break">1. Open the "Basic Shape Scene". 
<br class="ltx_break">2. Use the blue sphere as the reference point. Position the other two elements at a distance of 3 units from the reference along the X-axis, while preserving their original orientations. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"># RESULT FORMAT 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘json 
<br class="ltx_break">{"answer": "done"} 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
