<span id="A7.T13.3.28.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:17.3pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.28.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.28.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#FFECD9;">7</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.28.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.28.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.28.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.28.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"># Place a Torus on the Missing Axis 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## GOAL 
<br class="ltx_break">Identify the unoccupied axis in the XZ plane and place a new torus there, matching the distance of existing elements from the center. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## STEPS 
<br class="ltx_break">1. Open the "Four Objects Scene". 
<br class="ltx_break">2. Add a torus and place it along the only axis in the XZ plane that does not contain any existing element. Set its distance from the central point to be the same as that of the other elements. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"># RESULT FORMAT 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘json 
<br class="ltx_break">{"answer": "done"} 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
