</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.3.33" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.3.33.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFECD9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.33.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:17.3pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.33.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.33.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#FFECD9;">8</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.33.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.33.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.33.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.33.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"># Adjust Cube (Cuboid) Scale and Stack Cone 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## GOAL 
<br class="ltx_break">Modify the cuboid’s Y-axis scale and reposition it to rest on the XZ plane, then place the cone on top of the cuboid with proper surface contact. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## STEPS 
<br class="ltx_break">1. Open the “Four Objects Scene”. 
<br class="ltx_break">2. Set the cuboid’s scale along the Y-axis to 20, and adjust its position so that its bottom surface is in contact with the XZ plane. 
<br class="ltx_break">3. Adjust the position of the cone so that its bottom surface is in contact with the top surface of the cuboid, without overlap. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"># RESULT FORMAT 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘json 
<br class="ltx_break">{"answer": "done"} 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
