<td id="A7.T13.3.57.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.57.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.57.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;"><img src="2606.14397v1/images/3d_editor_gt_jpegs/tc_3d_editor_017.jpg" id="A7.T13.g22" class="ltx_graphics ltx_align_left ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/238;" width="476" height="238" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.3.58" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.3.58.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.58.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:17.3pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.58.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.58.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;">13</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.58.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.58.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.58.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.58.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"># Create Cube (Cuboid) with Scale Combinations 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## GOAL 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Find all possible integer scale combinations of a cube using the values 1, 2, and 4 on the x, y, and z axes. The three scale values must be assigned in all possible permutations, and each axis may be either positive or negative. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## STEPS 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">1. Open the "Empty Scene". 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">2. Create cubes (cuboids) for all possible combinations of scale values [1, 2, 4] across the x, y, and z axes, allowing each axis to be positive or negative. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">3. Set the position of each cube to (0, 0, 0) and assign all of them the same name, Cube 1. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## RESULT FORMAT 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘json 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">{"answer": "done"} 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.3.59" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.3.59.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.59.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.59.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.59.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.59.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Ground truth</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.3.60" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.3.60.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.60.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.60.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;"><img src="2606.14397v1/images/3d_editor_gt_jpegs/tc_3d_editor_013.jpg" id="A7.T13.g23" class="ltx_graphics ltx_align_left ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/238;" width="476" height="238" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.3.61" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.3.61.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.61.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:17.3pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.61.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.61.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;">14</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.61.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.61.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:300.2pt;">
<span id="A7.T13.3.61.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A7.T13.3.61.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"># Match Cone Volume to Cylinder and Stack 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## GOAL 
<br class="ltx_break">Adjust a cone’s Y-axis scale to match the cylinder’s volume, place the cone on top of the cylinder, and recolor both to red. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">## STEPS 
<br class="ltx_break">1. Open the “Four Objects Scene”. 
<br class="ltx_break">2. Adjust the cone so that its volume matches that of the cylinder by modifying only the scale along the Y-axis. The volume of the cylinder is given by <math id="A7.T13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\pi r^{2}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\pi r^{2}h</annotation></semantics></math>, and the volume of the cone is given by <math id="A7.T13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=(1/3)\pi r^{2}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=(1/3)\pi r^{2}h</annotation></semantics></math>. Determine the required Y-axis scaling factor to achieve equal volumes. Next, position the cone on top of the cylinder without any overlap. Finally, treat the cylinder and cone as a single object and change its color to red (#ff0000). 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"># RESULT FORMAT 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘json 
<br class="ltx_break">{"answer": "done"} 
<br class="ltx_break">‘‘‘</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A7.T13.3.62" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A7.T13.3.62.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFD9D9;padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"></td>
<td id="A7.T13.3.62.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
